# Hackedbox 0.8.8 — Change Log

## Core / Project Direction

* Continued the conversion and modernization of Hackedbox from its original Blackbox-derived codebase. now completed
* Continued replacing legacy Blackbox naming with Hackedbox naming throughout the source. completed.
* Continued conversion of legacy `.hh` headers to `.hpp`. completed
* Continued conversion of legacy `.cc` sources to `.cpp`. completed
* Updated copyright headers to:
  `Copyright (c) 2026 Kevin Day <blame582@gmail.com>`
  
* Removed obsolete build/source artifacts and legacy files as part of the conversion. completed

* Old Blackbox/Fluxbox styles are now considered incompatible with the current Hackedbox style implementation.

## Style System

* Replaced the original style handling with the new Hackedbox style system.
	this is the start of the New StyleEngine which will have support for the older styles files  
* Expanded style parsing and resource handling in `Screen`.
* Added/continued support for the new `.style` configuration format.
* Added support for `root.background` in style files.
* Background handling was moved to `hbsetbg`. no more color backgrounds
* Style resources now control more of the menu/window appearance rather than relying on legacy Blackbox-compatible behavior.
* Continued work on menu frame, title, text, texture, font, and color resources.
* Updated the Default style during the style-system conversion.
* Fixed and continued debugging style fallback behavior caused by resources not being read from the new format correctly.
* Menu colors and gradients were adjusted as part of the new style implementation.

## Background Handling

* Added `hbsetbg` as the Official Hackedbox Background setter. requires imlib2
* `root.background` is now used by `.style` files to specify the background command/path.
* `hbsetroot` is no longer being used as the image setter because it does not provide the required image functionality.
* Continued integration of `hbsetbg` into the Hackedbox configuration/style system.

## Runbox / Launcher

* Continued replacement of the old `hbrun` implementation.
* Reworked the launcher GUI and its integration with Hackedbox styling.
* Fixed the launcher progressing from a broken/white window to an actual empty launcher box when invoked from the menu.
* Continued debugging launcher focus, cursor, styling, and rendering behavior.

## Menu System

* Continued the new `MenuManager` implementation.
* Reworked menu initialization and menu-file handling in `HbScreen`.
* Continued migration of menu classes and resources to the Hackedbox naming/API scheme.
* Added/continued root-menu list management.
* Continued work on menu style resources including:

  * title font
  * frame texture
  * frame colors
  * text colors
  * highlighted/selected menu resources
  * justification
  * bullet configuration
* Continued debugging menu rendering and style-file resource loading.

## Screen / Resource Handling

* Continued modernization of `Screen.hpp` and `Screen.cpp`.
* Updated `HbScreen` resource structures for the current Hackedbox implementation.
* Added/continued handling for:

  * window styles
  * menu styles
  * focus behavior
  * auto raise
  * click raise
  * workspace configuration
  * placement policy
  * edge snapping threshold
  * row/column placement direction
  * background configuration
* Continued cleanup of legacy commented clock/date resource handling.
* Continued correction of header declarations so `Screen.hpp` matches the current `Screen.cpp` implementation.

## Configuration

* Continued migration away from the original Blackbox configuration assumptions.
* Configuration is increasingly based around Hackedbox-specific resources and behavior rather than maintaining compatibility with the original WM.
* Greenday was updated to use the current Hackedbox style/background system.

## HbTK

* Continued development of HbTK, the toolkit being built for Hackedbox.
* Continued development of native X/XLibre-based widgets without depending on GTK, Qt, or FLTK.
* Continued work on:

  * `Widget`
  * `MainWindow`
  * `Splitter`
  * `Painter`
  * terminal widgets
* Continued cleanup of internal class naming so HbTK is the toolkit name while its internal components do not unnecessarily use an `Hb` prefix.
* Continued work toward using HbTK for future Hackedbox applications.

## Terminally-Hacked

* Continued development of the native XLibre/X11 terminal.
* Continued use of Xft and Fontconfig for terminal font handling.
* Resolved the Fontconfig/Xft linking issue encountered during development.
* Continued development without Qt, GTK, or FLTK dependencies.

## Planned / Not Yet Completed

The following are **not counted as completed in 0.8.8**:

* Integrated Hackedbox hotkey system.
* Regional window snapping.
* 1/4 and 1/2 screen snapping/placement.
* Optional tiling-style placement.
* Integrated tray support inside the Hackedbox menu.
* Menu icon support.
* File manager.
* Hackedpad editor.
* Completion of Terminally-Hacked.
* Final replacement of the remaining external desktop applications.
* Final redesign of the overall Hackedbox architecture.

## Compatibility Status

Hackedbox 0.8.8 should be considered a substantially diverged descendant of the original Blackbox codebase.

Compatibility with:

* Blackbox styles — **not maintained**
* Fluxbox styles — **not maintained**
* Original Hackedbox legacy styles — **not maintained where incompatible with the new style system**
* crashes caused by window.font 

The project is now being developed around Hackedbox's own configuration, style, toolkit, and desktop-component architecture.

## Version

**Hackedbox 0.8.7**

This version represents the current development state of the project after the major style-system, menu, background, launcher, and toolkit changes.

The eventual **1.0** release should represent the point at which the current architecture is considered complete and stable rather than merely another incremental Blackbox-compatible release.



2026-08-23  Kevin Day <blame582@gmail.com>

	* Hackedbox 0.8.6:
	Begin major source and toolkit modernization following the 0.8.5
	release.

	* Core:
	Convert remaining Blackbox/B-prefixed source to Hackedbox/Hb
	naming. Rename .hh/.cc files to .hpp/.cpp and update includes.
	Update copyright headers and remove obsolete Blackbox/bbkeys
	components.

	* HbTK: started toolkit
	Add the HbTK toolkit and integrate it into the Hackedbox build.
	Add Application, Window, Widget, Dialog, Entry, Button, Frame,
	TitleBar, Splitter, Painter, Style, StyleEngine, Event and related
	components. Build HbTK as libhbtk.a and link it with Hackedbox.

	* Runbox:
	Add the HbTK-based Runbox and begin integrating it with Rootmenu.

	* Styles:
	Update style handling and introduce root.background for desktop
	background images.

	* hbsetbg:
	Add the Hackedbox hbsetbg image-setting utility with center, tile,
	stretch-to-center and stretch-to-edge modes. Replace old hsetbg
	usage and remove obsolete hbsetroot background handling.

	* Build system:
	Update Automake/autoconf configuration for HbTK and static-library
	building. Add RANLIB support and subdir-objects handling.

	* Documentation:
	Add hbsetbg documentation and update manual generation.

	* Menu:
	Updated menu execution handling and begin integration of the
	internal HbTK Runbox.

	* Current status:
	Hackedbox, HbTK and hbsetbg build successfully. Internal Runbox
	integration is not yet functional at runtime.
